module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulIdealOpenSubspace
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulRestrictedResolution
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.InternalHom.OpenSubspaceRestrictQuotient

/-!
# The restriction of a global quotient as the quotient the Koszul complex over an open resolves

The local-to-global step of [Stacks, Tag 0BQY] compares, over a member `U` of a cover, the
restriction of a resolution chosen on all of `X` with the Koszul complex of a sequence of
sections over `U`. `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.koszulRestrictedModelIso` and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.restrictedModelComparisonIso` carry out that
comparison from a hypothesis `θ` identifying the restriction of the global sheaf of modules with
the quotient formed over `U` by the Koszul morphism. **This file produces `θ`**, and so states
those two comparisons with `θ` discharged.

The global sheaf of modules is the quotient `O_X/I` by the sheaf of ideals a morphism `Φ` into
the structure sheaf generates — `CategoryTheory.Limits.cokernel` of `Φ`, which is what
`Stacks.RegularSequence.koszulQuotient` is. Restriction to `U` commutes with that quotient and
the resulting quotient over `U` is the one any morphism generating the same sheaf of ideals
there forms, which is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRestrictQuotientIsoOfSlice`; and the sheaf of ideals the
Koszul morphism of `f₁, …, f_r` generates on `X|_U` is, on sections, the one `f₁, …, f_r`
generate on the slice site, which is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections`.

**What is left is the local generation statement itself**: that `f₁, …, f_r` generate, over the
objects of `Opens X / U`, the sheaf of ideals that `Φ` generates on `X`. That is the hypothesis
`hgen` below. It is not a gap in the comparison but the tag's own local hypothesis — the content
of "`I` is locally generated by a regular sequence" — and it is the only input the three
definitions here take beyond what the global resolution supplies.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.koszulRestrictedQuotientIso`: **`θ` for the
  canonical Koszul morphism.** The restriction to `U` of the quotient of `O_X` by the sheaf of
  ideals `Φ` generates is the quotient the Koszul morphism of `f₁, …, f_r` forms on `X|_U`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.koszulRestrictedModelIsoOfGenerated` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.restrictedModelComparisonIsoOfGenerated`: the two
  comparisons of the models over `U` with `θ` discharged — the Koszul cochain complex over `U`
  and the restriction of a global resolution of the quotient present the same object of
  `D(O_{X|U})`, and have the same composition-product algebra as sheaves of graded algebras on
  `X|_U`.

## Implementation notes

**The hypothesis is read on the slice site.** Both sides of `hgen` are sheaves of ideals of the
slice structure sheaf `O_X|_U`: `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sliceIdealOfSections`
on the left and the one generated by the restriction of `Φ` on the right. That is the site on
which a comparison with a *global* sheaf of ideals can be stated at all — the restriction of `Φ`
to `X|_U` factors through it — and it is also the side on which
`sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections` leaves its conclusion, so the two meet with no
further transport.

**No `@[stacks]` attribute.** As in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulRestrictedResolution`, nothing here is a
clause of Tag 0BQY: this supplies an input to the gluing of the tag's local statements, not the
gluing itself. The caveats recorded on
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.forall_isIso_extComparison_of_isKoszulSequenceExactOn`
say what is still owed.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry HomologicalComplex Stacks.ChainComplex
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

open Stacks.Sites Stacks.SheafOfModules Stacks.RegularSequence
open Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {X : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (U : Opens X.carrier)
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : Opens X.carrier,
    HasWeakSheafify ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over V) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : Opens X.carrier,
    ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over V).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U))

/-- **The identification `θ` for the canonical Koszul morphism over `U`.** Let `Φ` be a morphism
into the structure sheaf of `X`, so that its cokernel is the quotient of `O_X` by the sheaf of
ideals `Φ` generates, and let `f₁, …, f_r` be sections of `O_X` over `U` which generate that
sheaf of ideals on the slice site over `U`. Then the restriction of the quotient to `X|_U` is
the quotient the Koszul morphism of `f₁, …, f_r`, read on `X|_U`, forms there.

This is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRestrictQuotientIsoOfSlice` with its hypothesis
supplied by `sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections` and `hgen`. -/
def koszulRestrictedQuotientIso {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)}
    (Φ : F ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing X))
    (hgen : ∀ W : (Over U)ᵒᵖ,
      sectionIdeal (sliceIdealOfSections U f) W =
        sectionIdeal (idealOfHom (O := X.sheaf.over U)
          ((_root_.SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (structureSheafRing X) U).map Φ)) W) :
    openSubspaceRestrictModule U (cokernel Φ) ≅
      quotient (openSubspace U).sheaf
        (φ := koszulHomOfSections (openSubspace U).sheaf
          fun j => sectionOnRestriction X U (f j)) :=
  openSubspaceRestrictQuotientIsoOfSlice U Φ _ fun V =>
    (sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections U f V).trans
      (hgen (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)))

variable
  {A : _root_.SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥(openSubspace U).carrier)
    (koszulFreeSheaf (openSubspace U).sheaf r)}
  (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A
    (koszulHomOfSections (openSubspace U).sheaf fun j => sectionOnRestriction X U (f j)))
  [QuasiIso K.augmentation]

/-- **The restriction to `U` of a resolution of the global quotient presents the object the
Koszul complex over `U` resolves**, with no hypothesis identifying the two quotients:
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.koszulRestrictedModelIso` at `θ` =
`koszulRestrictedQuotientIso`. -/
def koszulRestrictedModelIsoOfGenerated {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)}
    (Φ : F ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing X))
    (hgen : ∀ W : (Over U)ᵒᵖ,
      sectionIdeal (sliceIdealOfSections U f) W =
        sectionIdeal (idealOfHom (O := X.sheaf.over U)
          ((_root_.SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (structureSheafRing X) U).map Φ)) W)
    (I : CochainComplex (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)) ℤ) (hI : I.IsKInjective)
    (e : DerivedCategory.Q.obj
        ((single (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (cokernel Φ)) ≅
      DerivedCategory.Q.obj I) :
    DerivedCategory.Q.obj (cochain (openSubspace U).sheaf K) ≅
      DerivedCategory.Q.obj (openSubspaceRestrictComplex U I) :=
  koszulRestrictedModelIso U K (cokernel Φ) I hI e (koszulRestrictedQuotientIso U f Φ hgen)

/-- **The two models over `U` have the same composition-product algebra**, with no hypothesis
identifying the two quotients:
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.restrictedModelComparisonIso` at `θ` =
`koszulRestrictedQuotientIso`. This is the form in which the local-to-global step of
[Stacks, Tag 0BQY] needs the comparison. -/
def restrictedModelComparisonIsoOfGenerated {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)}
    (Φ : F ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing X))
    (hgen : ∀ W : (Over U)ᵒᵖ,
      sectionIdeal (sliceIdealOfSections U f) W =
        sectionIdeal (idealOfHom (O := X.sheaf.over U)
          ((_root_.SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (structureSheafRing X) U).map Φ)) W)
    (I : CochainComplex (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)) ℤ) (hI : I.IsKInjective)
    (e : DerivedCategory.Q.obj
        ((single (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (cokernel Φ)) ≅
      DerivedCategory.Q.obj I) :
    homologyGradedAlgebra (openSubspace U).sheaf (openSubspaceRestrictComplex U I) ≅
      homologyGradedAlgebra (openSubspace U).sheaf (cochain (openSubspace U).sheaf K) :=
  restrictedModelComparisonIso U K (cokernel Φ) I hI e
    (koszulRestrictedQuotientIso U f Φ hgen)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

end
